the number of reported coronavirus cases  in Louisiana is now skyrocketing  Omar Villafranca is in New Orleans at  the center of the state's outbreak Omar  what are officials there doing to stop  this virus spread good morning they shut  down Bourbon Street to cut back on the  crowds I mean take a look around me it  is empty one city council member is  comparing what happened here to what  happened in the aftermath of Hurricane  Katrina but keep in mind the French  Quarter State opened during Katrina and  now Governor John bel Edwards just wants  people to stay home we have to start  flattening the curve  Louisiana Governor John bel Edwards  sounded the alarm Wednesday as the surge  in corona virus cases threatens to  overwhelm state resources the problem  isn't just that the cases are growing  everyday it is that they're growing  rapidly every day officials estimate New  Orleans could run out of ventilators by  the first week of April  while hospitals are already racing to  find more personal protective equipment  we have never dealt with this number of  sick people dr. Rebecca key is the  former Louisiana state health secretary  what is it like right now for the  medical staff at hospitals there have  been told to conserve so for example  wear your mask during the day but if  it's not wet or soiled put it in a paper  bag and save it for tomorrow that is  unprecedented doctors and elected  officials believe the city's annual  Mardi Gras celebration help accelerate  the viruses spread  that's where Terra Reis believes her  husband Lewis was likely infected with  Koba 19 we were out on the streets with  hundreds and thousands of different  people two weeks later Lewis who is  undergoing chemotherapy for colon cancer  had a fever he later tested positive and  on Saturday was admitted to the  emergency room the doctor called me and  told me miss Reece we're gonna have to  put your husband and ICU and we are  gonna put him on a ventilator just  thinking about my husband being at the  hospital just all by himself Tara says  she was prepared for the worst but on  Monday she received a text from Lewis  himself who is currently on  the mend is like a miracle because he  really was really really sick supplies  are beginning to flow into the state the  governor is expecting a shipment of 300  ventilators but even with that shipment  he expects to be short about 600  ventilators just in the New Orleans area  Anthony Omar thank you
 

